    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "NODE Berlin Oslo is a graphic design studio founded in 2003 by Anders Hofgaard (NO) and Serge Rompza (DE), both Gerrit Rietveld Academy alumni. Two offices: Lindenstr. 90, Berlin (Rompza) and Mollergata 34B, Oslo (Hofgaard). Approx. 4 people per LinkedIn. Discipline focus: print, corporate identity, editorial, exhibition/environmental graphics, and web. Client base is strongly art/culture-institutional: Haus der Kulturen der Welt, Munch Museum, Astrup Fearnley, MIT Press, OMA, Diller Scofidio + Renfro, UN Environment Programme, Bundesministerium der Finanzen. Studio describes its approach as research-driven and context-sensitive rather than style-driven. Active teaching/workshop programme at European art academies (KHiO Oslo, UdK Berlin). Work Status sourced from node.international (studio entity, two principals) and LinkedIn company page. No individual Autonomy field set; org-type entry.",
      "source_url": null,
